# Code owners.
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR HERE. There is one maintainer, so this file assigns no work
# that would not have reached them anyway — every line names the same person.
# Its value is the second column of the comment: it records WHICH AUTHORITY
# GOVERNS EACH PATH, in a file GitHub puts in front of a reviewer automatically.
# A reviewer looking at a migration should be reminded that ADRs and the risk
# register decide what it may do, before reading the SQL and deciding it looks
# reasonable.
#
# It is therefore a map, not a rota. If a second maintainer ever appears, the
# ownership becomes real and the mapping is already written down.
#
# Later lines win, so the file runs general → specific.

# Default: everything.
*                                   @nickygregal12-cmyk

# ── Rules and decisions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Governed by docs/adr/**. A planning document never overrides an ADR, and the
# design authority may not change a scoring, lock, membership, settlement,
# progression or reveal rule.
/docs/adr/                          @nickygregal12-cmyk
/docs/scoring-rules.md              @nickygregal12-cmyk

# ── Live authorities ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One home each, and deliberately so. current-status.md is the ONLY live status
# authority; roadmap.md the only execution sequence; MASTER-TODO.md the only
# detailed inventory; accepted-requirements.md the only home for an accepted,
# unbuilt requirement — where a row is marked in place and never deleted.
/docs/quality/current-status.md     @nickygregal12-cmyk
/docs/quality/accepted-requirements.md @nickygregal12-cmyk
/docs/quality/risk-register.md      @nickygregal12-cmyk
/docs/roadmap.md                    @nickygregal12-cmyk
/MASTER-TODO.md                     @nickygregal12-cmyk
/AGENTS.md                          @nickygregal12-cmyk
/CLAUDE.md                          @nickygregal12-cmyk

# Generated, never hand-edited. `npm run check:now` fails on a manual change as
# well as on a stale one.
/NOW.md                             @nickygregal12-cmyk

# ── Immutable evidence ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dated audits, investigations and reconciliations are historical evidence at
# their recorded commit. They are corrected alongside, never rewritten to look
# current.
/docs/quality/audits/               @nickygregal12-cmyk
/docs/quality/investigations/       @nickygregal12-cmyk
/docs/quality/reconciliations/      @nickygregal12-cmyk
/docs/quality/history/              @nickygregal12-cmyk

# ── The database ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Append-only after hosted application. The repository contract is the migration
# COUNT, so a number cannot be reserved and one session at a time works here.
# Every new public table keeps RLS on; every security-definer function pins
# search_path; browser roles get minimum privileges.
/supabase/migrations/               @nickygregal12-cmyk
/supabase/tests/                    @nickygregal12-cmyk
/supabase/functions/                @nickygregal12-cmyk

# The machine-readable contract records. These are read by the deploy gates and
# by NOW.md; a hosted record is written by its rollout workflow, not by hand.
/config/                            @nickygregal12-cmyk

# ── Scoring and domain purity ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pure functions only: no storage, network or ambient clock; time is an input.
# competition/ may not import tournament/ or season/, and those two may not
# import each other. TypeScript and PostgreSQL scoring must agree — proven by
# tests/database-parity/, not by inspection.
/src/domain/                        @nickygregal12-cmyk
/tests/database-parity/             @nickygregal12-cmyk

# All browser database access goes through here, via bounded RPC/read-model
# contracts. Private integrity helpers are never exposed as browser RPCs.
/src/services/supabase/             @nickygregal12-cmyk

# ── Deployment and hosted state ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Headers, the route allowlist and the contract gate. Production deploys are
# paused by that gate by design; never weaken a guard to make a build pass.
/netlify.toml                       @nickygregal12-cmyk

# CI and the deploy gates. Production rollout workflows additionally require
# explicit owner approval and target-specific evidence — no agent touches them.
/.github/workflows/                 @nickygregal12-cmyk
/scripts/                           @nickygregal12-cmyk

# This file and the disclosure policy.
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @nickygregal12-cmyk
/SECURITY.md                        @nickygregal12-cmyk
